WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.295 --> 00:00:03.240
- Most people, when
they think of a jockey,

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:04.664
think of a male jockey.

00:00:04.664 --> 00:00:06.646
People who don't think
women can be jockeys

00:00:06.646 --> 00:00:07.855
are uneducated.

00:00:07.855 --> 00:00:10.857
Obviously, we are proving ourselves.

00:00:10.857 --> 00:00:12.367
I've become the first female jockey

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.253
to win the Melbourne Cup.

00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:18.003
It took 150 years for
a woman to finally win.

00:00:25.902 --> 00:00:28.091
My name is Michelle
Payne, and I am a jockey

00:00:28.091 --> 00:00:30.092
and horse trainer.

00:00:30.092 --> 00:00:34.213
Horse racing has been part of
our family before I was born.

00:00:34.213 --> 00:00:36.724
My dad was a jockey and a horse trainer,

00:00:36.724 --> 00:00:39.493
and my older brothers
and sisters all followed

00:00:39.493 --> 00:00:40.910
in his footsteps.

00:00:42.077 --> 00:00:43.204
I was very lucky growing up

00:00:43.204 --> 00:00:45.594
with a family, where,
it wasn't ever suggested

00:00:45.594 --> 00:00:48.249
that female jockeys couldn't
be as good as the male jockeys.

00:00:48.249 --> 00:00:51.082
And I think that really helped me.

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:56.311
The Melbourne Cup is the
race that stops the nation.

00:00:56.311 --> 00:00:59.263
It's such a huge event in Australia.

00:00:59.263 --> 00:01:02.543
As a jockey, it's what we all aim towards

00:01:02.543 --> 00:01:04.247
from as young as four or five years old

00:01:04.247 --> 00:01:06.470
it was basically my
dream to become a jockey

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:08.508
and to win the Melbourne Cup.

00:01:08.508 --> 00:01:10.519
So, I felt very privileged to have been

00:01:10.519 --> 00:01:13.433
the first female jockey to win.

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:16.683
(camera shutter snaps)

00:01:19.073 --> 00:01:20.458
It was a moment of disbelief.

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:22.433
It was a moment of years of training

00:01:22.433 --> 00:01:25.827
and dreaming of winning our
greatest race in Australia.

00:01:25.827 --> 00:01:27.994
It was an amazing feeling.

00:01:30.493 --> 00:01:32.729
I think the racing industry is great,

00:01:32.729 --> 00:01:34.909
because men and women compete equally

00:01:34.909 --> 00:01:37.919
and there's no separation
between one or the other.

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:39.647
In the generation coming through,

00:01:39.647 --> 00:01:41.823
we've got a lot more female apprentices,

00:01:41.823 --> 00:01:43.560
and I think that's fantastic.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:45.145
What I'd say to young children

00:01:45.145 --> 00:01:47.033
who would like to be a jockey:

00:01:47.033 --> 00:01:48.624
don't let people say you can't,

00:01:48.624 --> 00:01:50.927
because obviously, it is possible.

00:01:50.927 --> 00:01:52.486
That, for me, has been
the most important part

00:01:52.486 --> 00:01:54.047
of winning the Melbourne Cup.

00:01:54.047 --> 00:01:56.848
Showing and proving to
young girls coming through

00:01:56.848 --> 00:02:00.265
and current jockeys that it is possible.

